    "turn_text": "Well, it would be the equivalent. I mean, hate to me is, I don't even like the word. Is that his name? I don't even know he was. But here's the thing. I grew up as a Catholic, very devout Catholic family, and try to raise my own children the same way. You don't hate a person. You just don't. It's like you don't beat a person. So you couldn't have just as well been saying to me, did you beat your children before you came here today? It's just something so insulted and so shall we say projecting of where he was coming from himself. So I just think that in our country, I had this pin that I love, it's a flag, but it says one country, one destiny. And again, because all that our founders gave us in our exquisite constitution of the United States. They also gave us guidance. We played bassoonum for many one. We couldn't imagine how many we would be, how different we'd be. But they knew we always in all of our fights, and they fought curiously, our founders and those who came after them. You knew we had to always remember that we are one. So if the other side doesn't want to honor it's oath of office or if they're using words like hate to project their own attitudes on to somebody else, I just I have to draw the line and be the equipment of my saying to you. Did you starve your kids before you came here today? What are you talking about? I said to him, when you start talking about words like, hey, I'm a Catholic. Don't mess with me on that",
