    "turn_text": "It's over there, but hey. nothing surprising, who knows what people say, who knows what they mean. But you know what, this is not, this is not normal. I mean, we, we had, I've been speaker with President Bush, President, I disagreed vehemently with President Bush on the war in Iraq. What could be worse than that? What could be worse than that? And yet we had our other areas of agreement where we Barney Frank said the most progressive tax bill ever, giving refundability to the poorest families in America. We did PEPFAR. He wanted PEPFAR. We did PEPFAR. We did PEPFAR. We did so many things together. In fact, a couple of weeks ago, I was honored at a dinner in Washington. They said, we have a surprise for you. And it was a video from President Bush. And I was very moved by that. This thing about behavior that you would not really talk about in your own home much less the white house is very different. It isn't about being different. We have our differences. We come here believing what we believe. Confident in what we know about. Humble enough to listen to others. Recognizing we represent our districts. They represent their earth. So where do we find our common ground? We have a responsibility to seek it. Stand our ground where we can't. That would have been Thomas Jefferson, like a rock, where you can't find your common ground. But respectful always. This is quite different.",
