    "turn_idx": 70,
    "turn_text": "yes. But you know why? Because I always tell people, when 2016 happened, however you want to describe that, when that happened, people said to me, can you win the house in 218? I said, I'll tell you in November of 2017. And now in 2019, one year before the election, I can tell you, we will win the house. We don't take anything for granted. We own the ground, not yield one grain of sand in our mobilization. We message in a way that is progressive and mainstream, and we have the money to get it done. And we evaluate the performance of our members of Congress, of whom we are very proud from their official performance and duties and politically what we can do working together. Versus, when I say to anybody who might want to run against one of our candidates, your president is under 50%. Our candidates are formidable. They've done their official duties. We're going to own the ground. We've had Jerry Bustos who's had people out there for 10 months already messaging all that. You might want to think about this for another time as we fully intend to win. And if it's an incumbent, we say to them, you're going to have a race. It's going to cost you. You're going to have to explain your votes to suburban America. You've never really had to defend your votes here. You're going to now. Your president's under 50%. You may want to spend more time with your family. So we have in the high 20s of retirements, and we feel very good about the strength of our incumbents versus the field that is out there against them. So in any event, again, after that, we'll work together. Declary bassoonum.",
